prompt:
Build ONE self-contained HTML file: a playable lunar lander game rendered on <canvas data-testid="simulation">. Moon gravity 1.62 m/s^2. Controls: up-arrow or W for thrust, left/right or A/D to rotate; thrust burns fuel proportionally. Terrain is generated deterministically from a seed and contains one flat landing pad. HUD shows altitude (m), vertical speed vy (m/s, NEGATIVE when descending), horizontal speed vx (m/s), fuel (%), tilt (deg). Touchdown is a SUCCESS only if |vy| <= 3, |vx| <= 2 and |tilt| <= 15 deg; otherwise it crashes/explodes. On success show a score computed from remaining fuel and distance to pad center in <div data-testid="score"></div>.

MANDATORY benchmark API — a hidden automated grader calls exactly this; it must exist on window before load finishes and be independent of wall-clock time:
window.BENCH = {
  reset(seed) {},              // regenerate terrain from seed; lander at x = center, altitude 400 m, vy = vx = 0, tilt 0, fuel 100, crashed = landed = false
  step(ms) {},                 // advance physics by exactly ms milliseconds of simulated time (fixed-dt substeps)
  perform(action, payload) {}, // 'thrust' with {level: 0..1} sets engine level until changed; 'rotate' with {deg: number} sets tilt
  getState() { return {seed, crashed, landed, timeMs}; },
  getMetrics() { return {altitude, vy, vx, fuel, tiltDeg}; }
};
Include <button data-testid="reset">Reset</button> wired to BENCH.reset(1). The game must also animate and be playable normally via requestAnimationFrame when the grader is not driving it. No external libraries — plain canvas 2D and vanilla JS only.
